PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round 0 debate centers on NI 45-106 AI tests: individuals (income >200k solo/>300k joint for both prior years + expectation; net financial assets >1M; net assets >=5M) vs. entities (net assets >=5M on FS or all direct/indirect interest owners are themselves AIs). 

Colleagues split 3-2-1: 1 & 5 pick A (LP fails entity tests due to corporate GP whose status/ownership chain is unclear, blocking "all owners AIs" safe harbour); 2,3,4 pick E (Alex/Bob not AIs so entity route unavailable; corp's net assets ~5.2M unconfirmed once investment-property values/liabilities factored in, and "solely to hold financial assets" purpose not shown); 6 picks B (2019 joint income 320k arguably insufficiently above threshold). 

Key evidence preserved: A’s GP received 6M (likely qualifies it as AI entity itself); C hits exactly 5M net assets; D received 10M cash; E’s owners fail individual tests outright. Unresolved: whether GP ownership look-through applies cleanly for A and whether E’s undisclosed property values could still reach 5M. Current lean: E is the only choice that definitively fails both entity routes on the facts given.}

